  :adr/body
  "# ADR-2607198100: Hash-bound Kotoba source verification before Q9 migration

**Status**: accepted
**Date**: 2026-07-19

## Decision

A non-comment `.kotoba` file is no longer called canonical merely from its
first line. Its exact SHA-256 source must pass frontend analysis, inferred
least-capability admission, and at least one declared compilation target.
Kernel intrinsics select only the AIUEOS kernel target; other candidates are
checked on Wasm and JavaScript. Q9 tranches reject every repository containing
a DSL collision, stale/unverified proof, or a source rejected by all selected
targets.

The current audit classified all 1,017 bare-extension paths: 779 legacy
schema DSL collisions, 13 archived legacy-language collisions, 223
compiler/runtime/project-verified canonical sources, two hash-bound fixtures,
and zero rejected candidates. The former five oversized kernel sources are
retained as non-bare `.kotoba-bundle` authoring inputs and deterministically
lowered into 19 independent `.kotoba` components. Each component has at most
900 source functions, balanced associative addition trees, and pure high-arity
helpers inlined at their call sites before compiler admission.

The audit also exposed an internal Wasm NPE for AIUEOS kernel memory
intrinsics. Compilation now rejects such operations before entering an
incompatible backend and reports a structured target-phase error.

## Soak

Fresh GitHub evidence collection found zero matching main-push runs for all ten
Wave 1 tranche repositories because their qualification revisions remain on
rescue branches. The soak and consumer-cutover gates therefore remain closed."}]
